//! Log and exponential tables for the tower's `GF(2^8)`.
//!
//! The multiplicative group of `GF(2^8)` is cyclic of order `255`, generated by
//! [`BinaryField8::GENERATOR`]. Writing every nonzero element as `g^e`, a product is a sum of
//! exponents, so a multiplication is two [`LOG`] lookups, an addition and one [`EXP`] lookup,
//! and an inversion is a negation of the exponent between the same two lookups.
//!
//! The tables are pinned constants; `regenerate_tables` in the test module below derives them
//! from [`BinaryField8::reference_mul`] and checks them against what is written here.
//!
//! [`BinaryField8::GENERATOR`]: crate::BinaryField8
//! [`BinaryField8::reference_mul`]: crate::BinaryField8::reference_mul

/// `LOG[x]` is the exponent `e < 255` with `GENERATOR^e = x`, for every nonzero `x`.
///
